<p>(a) In June 1996, the company incurred an extraordinary charge of $54,000 net of income tax benefit of $34,000, for the write-off of unamortized deferred financing costs, unamortized original issue discount, and certain premium on reacquisition associated with the repurchase of $500,000 of senior secured notes due 2002.  In the fourth quarter of 1995, the company redeemed $24 million in principal amount of its outstanding senior notes with the net proceeds from its initial public offering.  In connection with the redemption, the company recorded a $2.9 million extraordinary charge (net of tax benefit) resulting from the 11.4 per cent cash call premium and the related write-off of unamortized original discount and deferred financing costs.</p>
